{"test_id": "B13-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence should a Risk Manager prepare to demonstrate board cybersecurity oversight?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Board minutes must show cybersecurity as regular agenda item", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}, {"fact": "Evidence of board decisions on security investments and risk acceptance", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}, {"fact": "Minutes should be signed or otherwise authenticated", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Board cybersecurity oversight**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Governance (Section 8)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Board meeting minutes\n- Cybersecurity presentation decks\n- Board-approved policies\n- Risk register reviews\n- Investment approvals\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Board minutes must show cybersecurity as regular agenda item** (critical priority)\n- **Evidence of board decisions on security investments and risk acceptance** (critical priority)\n- **Minutes should be signed or otherwise authenticated** (important priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 8, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Governance", "Map to CCoP Section 8", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evidence specifics", "Specific evidence types required", "Evidence quality considerations", "Organization and preparation guidance"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific CSA evidence forms", "Creating non-existent evidence requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "8", "clause_reference": ["8.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "evidence_preparation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B13-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What documentation demonstrates complete CII asset inventory?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Asset register must include OT systems and shadow IT", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "Data flow maps show how information moves between systems", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "Inventory should be dated with version control", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: CII asset inventory completeness**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Identification (Section 4)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Asset register with all systems\n- Data flow diagrams\n- Network topology maps\n- Asset classification schema\n- Inventory update procedures\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Asset register must include OT systems and shadow IT** (critical priority)\n- **Data flow maps show how information moves between systems** (critical priority)\n- **Inventory should be dated with version control** (important priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 4, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Identification", "Map to CCoP Section 4", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapor