{"test_id": "B13-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence shows that risk assessments inform security priorities?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Risk register must be current and dated", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "Methodology should show systematic risk evaluation process", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "Risk acceptance decisions must be formally documented", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Risk assessment documentation**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Identification (Section 4)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Risk register\n- Risk assessment methodology\n- Risk assessment reports\n- Control selection justification\n- Residual risk acceptance\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Risk register must be current and dated** (critical priority)\n- **Methodology should show systematic risk evaluation process** (critical priority)\n- **Risk acceptance decisions must be formally documented** (important priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 4, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Identification", "Map to CCoP Section 4", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evi