{"test_id": "B13-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What documentation demonstrates physical security implementation?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Access logs must show physical entry monitoring", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 5"}, {"fact": "Badge system records must be reviewed for anomalies", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 5"}, {"fact": "Camera coverage maps should show critical areas covered", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 5"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Physical security controls**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Protection (Section 5)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Physical security policy\n- Access logs\n- Camera coverage maps\n- Badge system records\n- Guard tour logs\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Access logs must show physical entry monitoring** (critical priority)\n- **Badge system records must be reviewed for anomalies** (important priority)\n- **Camera coverage maps should show critical areas covered** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 5, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Protection", "Map to CCoP Section 5", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evidence specifics", "Specific evide