{"test_id": "B13-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence shows awareness of regulatory requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Compliance calendar must track all CCoP requirements", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "Regulatory updates should be reviewed and incorporated", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}, {"fact": "CSA correspondence shows active regulatory engagement", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 4"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Legal and regulatory compliance tracking**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Identification (Section 4)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Compliance calendar\n- Regulatory update reviews\n- Legal consultation records\n- Compliance certifications\n- CSA correspondence\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Compliance calendar must track all CCoP requirements** (critical priority)\n- **Regulatory updates should be reviewed and incorporated** (important priority)\n- **CSA correspondence shows active regulatory engagement** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 4, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Identification", "Map to CCoP Section 4", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Sin