{"test_id": "B13-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence shows threat intelligence informs security decisions?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Threat intelligence feeds must be integrated into monitoring", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 6"}, {"fact": "Threat briefings should inform security priorities", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 6"}, {"fact": "IOC lists should be used for detection tuning", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 6"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Threat intelligence utilization**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Detection (Section 6)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Threat intelligence subscriptions\n- Threat reports\n- Indicator IOC lists\n- Threat briefings\n- Adjustment to threats\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Threat intelligence feeds must be integrated into monitoring** (critical priority)\n- **Threat briefings should inform security priorities** (important priority)\n- **IOC lists should be used for detection tuning** (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 6, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Detection", "Map to CCoP Section 6", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evidence speci