{"test_id": "B13-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence shows forensic investigation readiness?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Forensic retainer ensures specialist access when needed", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 7"}, {"fact": "Evidence collection procedures must preserve chain of custody", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 7"}, {"fact": "Tools inventory shows capability to collect evidence", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 7"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: Forensic investigation capability**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Response (Section 7)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- Forensic tools inventory\n- Forensic retainer agreements\n- Evidence collection procedures\n- Forensic training certificates\n- Past investigation reports\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **Forensic retainer ensures specialist access when needed** (critical priority)\n- **Evidence collection procedures must preserve chain of custody** (critical priority)\n- **Tools inventory shows capability to collect evidence** (important priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 7, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Response", "Map to CCoP Section 7", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evidence specifics", "Specific evidence types required", "Evidence quality considerations", "Organization and preparation guidance"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific CSA evidence forms", "Creating non-existent evidence requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "evidence_preparation", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B13-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B13", "input": {"question": "What evidence shows proper CII designation maintenance?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CII designation letter from CSA is foundational document", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}, {"fact": "Material changes must be reported to CSA", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}, {"fact": "Scope documentation must be current and accurate", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8"}], "expected_response": "**Evidence Requirements for: CII designation documentation**\n\n**CCoP Domain:** Governance (Section 8)\n\n**Required Evidence Types:**\n- CII designation letter\n- Scope documentation\n- Material change notifications\n- CSA confirmation of scope\n- Annual compliance submission\n\n\n**Evidence Quality Dimensions:**\n- **CII designation letter from CSA is foundational document** (critical priority)\n- **Material changes must be reported to CSA** (critical priority)\n- **Scope documentation must be current and accurate** (important priority)\n\n\n**Preparation Timeline:**\nEvidence should be collected and organized at least 30 days before audit submission. All evidence should be:\n- **Complete:** Covers all aspects of the control\n- **Current:** Dated within appropriate timeframes\n- **Authentic:** Verifiable as genuine and unaltered\n\n**Organization Tip:**\nCreate an evidence folder structure organized by CCoP section to facilitate audit preparation and ongoing maintenance.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 Section 8, CIIO Audit Evidence Requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify domain: Governance", "Map to CCoP Section 8", "Determine what evidence auditors require"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating any evidence is sufficient without quality requirements", "Downplaying evidence currency or authenticity", "Ignoring Singapore audit evidence specifics", "Specific e